Track 1: Dockmaster Osei’s Fata Morgana
- Story & Context: On October 14, 1985, Dockmaster Osei sat in the rust-flaked watchtower of Tema Port as a sudden maritime whiteout smothered the Gulf of Guinea, blurring three 40,000-ton bulk carriers into looming, spectral mirages hovering above the water. When the lead vessel blast its low D typhon horn into the salt air, Osei instinctively triggered his Oberheim DMX and twin 1960s Fender Stratocasters through the port’s PA, returning the bellow with a lightning-fast pentatonic arpeggio that made the harbor cranes shudder. The ships began answering the interlocking highlife guitars with synchronized, reverberant horn blasts, igniting a three-hour nocturnal dialogue that startled customs officers and birthed a new sonic dialect. His broadcast microphone caught the opening cry that codified the genre’s first maritime communion: "Signal through the gray, let the deep keel chime."
