Track 3: Freezing Cranes Swallow The Circumzenithal Arc
- Story & Context: Decades after the great November squall of 1989, maritime scavengers still gather at the abandoned container slips of Keta where three grounded freighters sit rusted together like an iron cathedral under cold prismatic skies. Local folklore swears that whenever a rare circumzenithal arc appears inverted like an upside-down rainbow above the clouds, the salt-rotted mechanical winches tension themselves and release a deafening, gated snare strike that carries fifty miles out to sea. Retired dockworkers pour tall glasses of palm spirit onto the tide-washed steel plates, clapping out the syncopated 3:2 rhythms as distant navigational buoys hum an impossible electronic counter-melody across the Atlantic deep. In the silence between the waves, the surviving chorus echoes from the hollowed hull walls: "The sky bends back to see the iron dance."
